From 2b42d72f8be71bc88b7abb9f51675006972b6ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VsRocq contributor <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:30:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] language-server: enforce vsrocq.memory.limit on running
 computations

`vsrocq.memory.limit` only triggered a `Gc.compact`/purge of closed
documents; it never bounded an in-flight computation, and the
`memprof-limits` dependency was wired for cancellation only. A single
`Compute` producing a large value could therefore grow `vsrocqtop`
without bound until the host ran out of memory.

- proverThread: run every job under `Memprof_limits.limit_global_memory`
  (nested with the existing cancellation token), set the global limit
  from the configuration, and report a memory abort as `Aborted` after
  compacting the heap.
- checkingManager/lspManager: plumb `vsrocq.memory.limit` (GB -> kiB)
  through to proverThread.
- executionManager: turn `Aborted` into a sentence error instead of
  raising in the event loop, which used to kill the server.
- tests/docs: add a regression test and correct the setting's description.
